data: {"type":"toolResult","tool_result":{"call":{"provider":"call_RBLcvFkJdKP7coFetBCN0dIA"},"name":"search_world","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Glass Aqueduct (aqueduct) [ID: 0a05f0fd-2132-40c5-b10c-63a7f2b9d187]: The Glass Aqueduct once ran from the Basalt Hills to feed the Sablecross reservoir. The Sablecross council owns it. Mira Venn maintained it before its permanent destruction by a landslide in 204. It has not been rebuilt, and there is no alternate aqueduct or bypass.\n  Properties: alternate_aqueduct_or_bypass: false; destroyed_in: 204; destruction_cause: landslide; destruction_permanent: true; rebuilt: false; source_conversation: 01a18777-7744-715a-a990-daf20fc93f3f\n  - ← MAINTAINS from Mira Venn (person, engineer) [ID: 7d2fec61-8487-4192-8bf3-db75accaaa8f]: An engineer who maintained the Glass Aqueduct before its destruction in 204. She was born in Greyhaven, a small town on the coast, and moved to Sablecross as an adult. She keeps a cracked jade compass inside her right boot; only her friend Oren Dask knows about it.\n  - ← OWNS from Sablecross council (council, governing body) [ID: ccb30b2e-6e33-42d7-a6d2-a754da506f10]: The owner of the Glass Aqueduct.\n  - ← PLANS_FOR from Original aqueduct plans (plans, document) [ID: d5476f0a-57e4-43dc-b873-003fd4024e30]: The original aqueduct plans, kept in the Sun Archive.\n  - FEEDS → Sablecross reservoir (reservoir) [ID: 2a3ca8de-f578-4c53-a2cf-78f147162aee]: A reservoir in Sablecross, historically fed by the Glass Aqueduct before its destruction in 204.\n  - RUNS_FROM → Basalt Hills (hills, geographic feature) [ID: 2ec99b4b-9d81-4b3e-8da3-e77d88559be1]: Hills from which the Glass Aqueduct comes.\n\nSablecross reservoir (reservoir) [ID: 2a3ca8de-f578-4c53-a2cf-78f147162aee]: A reservoir in Sablecross, historically fed by the Glass Aqueduct before its destruction in 204.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18777-7744-715a-a990-daf20fc93f3f\n  - ← FEEDS from Glass Aqueduct (aqueduct) [ID: 0a05f0fd-2132-40