ass, object) [ID: 7e23d4d7-7bfd-4ce7-9db3-91d1ebe3ee71]: A cracked jade compass that Mira Venn keeps inside her right boot. Only her friend Oren Dask knows about it.\n  - BORN_IN → Greyhaven (town, coastal settlement) [ID: 70ce38c9-4472-43bc-8fd0-7733401ad249]: A small town on the coast.\n\nSablecross council (council, governing body) [ID: ccb30b2e-6e33-42d7-a6d2-a754da506f10]: The owner of the Glass Aqueduct.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18777-7744-715a-a990-daf20fc93f3f\n  - OWNS → Glass Aqueduct (aqueduct) [ID: 0a05f0fd-2132-40c5-b10c-63a7f2b9d187]: The Glass Aqueduct once ran from the Basalt Hills to feed the Sablecross reservoir. The Sablecross council owns it. Mira Venn maintained it before its permanent destruction by a landslide in 204. It has not been rebuilt, and there is no alternate aqueduct or bypass.\n\nOriginal aqueduct plans (plans, document) [ID: d5476f0a-57e4-43dc-b873-003fd4024e30]: The original aqueduct plans, kept in the Sun Archive.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18777-7744-715a-a990-daf20fc93f3f\n  - ← CONTAINS from Sun Archive (archive) [ID: e7e97d97-f1a0-4a74-98e5-6f4cd1c78282]: The Sun Archive is kept by Lysa Renn, contains the original aqueduct plans, and admits civilian scholars during daylight only.\n  - PLANS_FOR → Glass Aqueduct (aqueduct) [ID: 0a05f0fd-2132-40c5-b10c-63a7f2b9d187]: The Glass Aqueduct once ran from the Basalt Hills to feed the Sablecross reservoir. The Sablecross council owns it. Mira Venn maintained it before its permanent destruction by a landslide in 204. It has not been rebuilt, and there is no alternate aqueduct or bypass."}]}}

